      <div class="chapter-line"><span class="chapter-n" aria-hidden="true">04</span><p class="chapter-name" aria-hidden="true">What changed</p><span class="chapter-rule" aria-hidden="true"></span></div>
      <h2 id="result-title" class="claim"><span class="visually-hidden">What changed: </span>Paper’s out. It’s running in pilot clubs.</h2>
      <div class="prose-narrow">
        <p>When I left, the app was in pilot at a few clubs, already cutting weeks off precounts and tightening up variance.</p>
        <p>The people using it wanted it. In testing, associates and managers were excited to see the “archaic” paper process go, and moved through both flows with little confusion.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="result-row">
        <div class="results">
